{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-5e7066c8-dc79-4f35-88aa-83d697e8173c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a981539e242dd82e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9019-e56dyfuc/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9019-E001.md","content":"# Dashboard tutorial gallery and one-click launch mechanics\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers the tutorial gallery in the Dashboard: a curated, browsable set of\ngetting-started tutorials that a user can launch into their own project with\none click. Notebook tutorials open a workbench in the user's project with the\ntutorial notebook loaded; pipeline tutorials import the pipeline into the\nuser's project. The gallery reads tutorial packages conforming to the tutorial\npackaging format (package metadata and pinned images), so tutorial content can\nbe updated and versioned without Dashboard releases. This addresses the\nblank-platform problem: today the first workbench, first pipeline, and first\nmodel deployment all start from empty forms.\n\n## Scope\n\n- A tutorial gallery section in the Dashboard (navigation entry, tutorial\n  listing, and tutorial detail view) backed by tutorial packages conforming to\n  the tutorial packaging format.\n- One-click launch mechanics:\n  - Notebook tutorials: open a workbench in the user's project with the\n    tutorial notebook loaded, using the pinned image the package specifies.\n  - Pipeline tutorials: import the pipeline into the user's project.\n- Gallery surfaced where new users land in the Dashboard so the curated set is\n  discoverable at first login (time-to-first-success is the strategy's driver).\n- Ability to enable/disable the gallery through Dashboard configuration,\n  consistent with existing per-component feature flags administered via\n  `OdhDashboardConfig`.\n- Incidental UI copy and help-text updates that fall out of the gallery change\n  (no new documentation content — that is authored separately).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a user with a project, when they open the tutorial gallery, the\n  curated tutorial set is listed with its package metadata (title, journey,\n  tutorial type).\n- Given a notebook tutorial package conforming to the tutorial packaging\n  format, when the user launches it from the gallery, a workbench opens in\n  their project with the tutorial notebook loaded and the package's pinned\n  image selected.\n- Given a pipeline tutorial package conforming to the tutorial packaging\n  format, when the user launches it from the gallery, the pipeline is imported\n  into the user's project.\n- Launch flows are verified against tutorial packages that conform to the\n  packaging format (including the curated set once it is available).\n- The gallery can be enabled and disabled through Dashboard configuration\n  without a code change.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: \"The Dashboard has a tutorial gallery from which a user can\n  launch a tutorial into their project (opening a workbench with the notebook,\n  or importing the pipeline).\" — Fully covered by this epic: the gallery UI and\n  both launch flows. Also provides the launchability that the curated tutorial\n  set depends on.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47080,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-867e6a62c2163417","agent_id":"ad4900b91d8d01234","session_id":"d7ee07fb-436c-408b-a521-661a0ee22d32","uuid":"b6605a57-0e52-4e4e-bafd-a8b3bc64ff3d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:35:36.237Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019 into epics"}
