{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-5e7066c8-dc79-4f35-88aa-83d697e8173c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-80212b22232e522d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9019-e56dyfuc/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9019-E002.md","content":"# Tutorial packaging format and validation harness\n\n## Description\n\nDefines the tutorial packaging format that makes tutorials versioned and\ntestable independently of Dashboard releases, and delivers the validation\nharness that executes a package's validation manifest. A tutorial package\ncarries metadata describing the tutorial, references to pinned images, and a\nvalidation manifest; the harness runs that manifest so any tutorial can be\ntested against a target release on demand, without coupling tutorial releases\nto Dashboard releases.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Format specification for tutorial packages:\n  - Package metadata describing the tutorial (title, core journey, tutorial\n    type — notebook or pipeline, entry point).\n  - Pinned image references (the platform-maintained workbench images the\n    tutorial runs on).\n  - A validation manifest describing how the tutorial is tested.\n- Versioning rules that let tutorial packages be published and updated\n  independently of Dashboard releases.\n- A validation harness that executes a package's validation manifest against a\n  target release and reports pass/fail.\n- A reference (sample) package that demonstrates the format end to end.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The packaging format defines package metadata, pinned-image references, and\n  a validation manifest for tutorial packages.\n- A tutorial package can be versioned and published without requiring a\n  Dashboard release.\n- The validation harness executes a package's validation manifest and produces\n  a pass/fail result, demonstrated with the reference package against a target\n  release.\n-