a workbench in the user's project with the\n51\t    tutorial notebook loaded, using the pinned image the package specifies.\n52\t  - Pipeline tutorials: import the pipeline into the user's project.\n53\t- Gallery surfaced where new users land in the Dashboard so the curated set is\n54\t  discoverable at first login (time-to-first-success is the strategy's driver).\n55\t- Ability to enable/disable the gallery through Dashboard configuration,\n56\t  consistent with existing per-component feature flags administered via\n57\t  `OdhDashboardConfig`.\n58\t- Incidental UI copy and help-text updates that fall out of the gallery change\n59\t  (no new documentation content — that is authored separately).\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Given a user with a project, when they open the tutorial gallery, the\n64\t  curated tutorial set is listed with its package metadata (title, journey,\n65\t  tutorial type).\n66\t- Given a notebook tutorial package conforming to the tutorial packaging\n67\t  format, when the user launches it from the gallery, a workbench opens in\n68\t  their project with the tutorial notebook loaded and the package's pinned\n69\t  image selected.\n70\t- Given a pipeline tutorial package conforming to the tutorial packaging\n71\t  format, when the user launches it from the gallery, the pipeline is imported\n72\t  into the user's project.\n73\t- Launch flows are verified against tutorial packages that conform to the\n74\t  packaging format (including the curated set once it is available).\n75\t- The gallery can be enabled and disabled through Dashboard configuration\n76\t  without a code change.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: \"The Dashboard has a tutorial gallery from which a user can\n81\t  launch a tutorial into their project (opening a workbench with the notebook,\n82\t  or importing the pipeline).\" — Fully covered by this epic: the gallery UI and\n83\t  both launch flows. Also provides the launchability that the 