{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0dd9dd26fffd077","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9019-E002\n3\ttitle: Tutorial packaging format and validation harness\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n5\tcomponent: Notebooks\n6\tteam: Workbenches\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: -1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 0\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 0\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 2\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Tutorial packaging format and validation harness\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tDefines the tutorial packaging format that makes tutorials versioned and\n34\ttestable independently of Dashboard releases, and delivers the validation\n35\tharness that executes a package's validation manifest. A tutorial package\n36\tcarries metadata describing the tutorial, references to pinned images, and a\n37\tvalidation manifest; the harness runs that manifest so any tutorial can be\n38\ttested against a target release on demand, without coupling tutorial releases\n39\tto Dashboard releases.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Format specification for tutorial packages:\n44\t  - Package metadata describing the tutorial (title, core journey, tutorial\n45\t    type — notebook or pipeline, entry point).\n46\t  - Pinned image references (the platform-maintained workbench images the\n47\t    tutorial runs on).\n48\t  - A validation manifest describing how the tutorial is tested.\n49\t- Versioning rules that let tutorial packages be published and updated\n50\t  independently of Dashboard releases.\n51\t- A validation harness that executes a package's validation manifest against a\n52\t  target release and reports pass/fail.\n53\t- A reference (sample) package that demonstrates the format end to end.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The packaging format defines package metadata, pinned-image references, and\n58\t  a validation manifest for tutorial packages.\n59\t- A tutorial package can be versioned and published without requiring a\n60\t  Dashboard release.\n61\t- The validation harness executes a package's validation manifest and produces\n62\t  a pass/fail result, demonstrated with the reference package against a target\n63\t  release.\n64\t- Packages can pin the platform-maintained workbench images so tutorial runs\n65\t  are reproducible.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: \"A tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images,\n70\t  validation manifest) is defined so tutorials are versioned and testable\n71\t  independently of Dashboard releases.\" — Fully covered by this epic. The\n72\t  strategy labels the HLR P1, but the epic's priority is promoted to P0 by\n73\t  priority inheritance: the Dashboard gallery consumes the format and the\n74\t  curated tutorials are packaged and validated per it, so it enables all P0\n75\t  work in this strategy (promotion recorded as a health warning in the\n76\t  decomposition summary).\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1fcb1811e2242eb","agent_id":"a78112c6760456c14","session_id":"d7ee07fb-436c-408b-a521-661a0ee22d32","uuid":"ec976648-f71a-4aca-b484-59a9606a5e36","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:37:50.378Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0dd9dd26fffd077","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
