{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b67601ea04bcf91a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tepic_count: 4\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9019: Curated getting-started tutorial gallery\n10\t\n11\t## Strategy Overview\n12\t\n13\tThe strategy delivers a curated tutorial gallery in the Dashboard: maintained,\n14\ttested tutorials (notebooks and pipelines) that users launch into their own\n15\tproject with one click. The problem statement itself identifies three\n16\tarchitecturally distinct work streams with different owners and review\n17\tprocesses: product code (gallery and launch mechanics), authored content (the\n18\ttutorials), and documentation. No open questions, no external dependencies,\n19\tno Staff Engineer Input section.\n20\t\n21\t## Step 0 Triage Record\n22\t\n23\tTriage evaluated and **not triggered**. The strategy is not S-sized\n24\tsingle-component single-team work: it spans multiple components (Dashboard,\n25\tNotebooks, Data Science Pipelines, Documentation) and, per the strategy's own\n26\tproblem statement, multiple distinct work streams — code implementation,\n27\tsubstantive content authoring (six new tutorials), and documentation. The\n28\tmultiple-work-streams escape condition applies; full decomposition follows.\n29\t\n30\t## Component Classification\n31\t\n32\t| Component | Classification | Handling |\n33\t|-----------|----------------|----------|\n34\t| Dashboard | Active (code changes: gallery UI + launch mechanics) | Implementation epic E001 |\n35\t| Notebooks | Passive (no notebook-controller changes indicated; tutorials run on workbenches) | Validation ACs on E001 (workbench opens with notebook, pinned image) and E003 (notebook tutorials run in workbenches) |\n36\t| Data Science Pipelines | Passive (pipeline tutorials import via existing KFP v2 surfaces) | Validation AC on E003 (pipeline tutorial imports and runs) |\n37\t| Documentation | Docs content work | `docs-authoring` epic E004 |\n38\t\n39\t**Component mapping notes** (canonical names from `.context/rhai-components.txt`):\n40\t\n41\t- E002 (packaging format) and E003 (tutorials) both map to canonical\n42\t  `Notebooks`: the tutorials are primarily notebooks launched into workbenches,\n43\t  and the format's pinned images are the platform-maintained workbench images\n44\t  (see `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/notebooks.md`).\n45\t- E003's work spans `Data Science Pipelines` (the first-pipeline tutorial is a\n46\t  pipeline definition imported via KFP v2); the span is recorded here and the\n47\t  DSP-side validation is an acceptance criterion on E003 rather than a separate\n48\t  epic — the strategy frames the tutorials as one curated, tested set.\n49\t- E002's format is consumed by the Dashboard gallery (E001's code parses the\n50\t  package metadata); this cross-component consumption is captured by the\n51\t  E002 → E001 DAG edge, not by combining component names.\n52\t\n53\t## Epic List\n54\t\n55\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n56\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n57\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Dashboard tutorial gallery and one-click launch mechanics | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P0 |\n58\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Tutorial packaging format and validation harness | Implementation | Workbenches | Notebooks | P0 |\n59\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Six curated getting-started tutorials | Implementation | Workbenches | Notebooks | P0 |\n60\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Tutorial gallery usage and contribution documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | Documentation | P1 |\n61\t\n62\tE004's priority is P1 per the `docs-authoring` priority exception: the\n63\tstrategy frontmatter priority is `Major` (Major → P1), overriding the P2 label\n64\ton its HLR. Docs edges do not push priority upstream.\n65\t\n66\t## Dependency DAG\n67\t\n68\t```mermaid\n69\tgraph TD\n70\t    E002[\"E002 Tutorial packaging format + validation harness\"] --> E001[\"E001 Dashboard gallery + launch mechanics\"]\n71\t    E002 --> E003[\"E003 Six curated tutorials\"]\n72\t    E001 --> E004[\"E004 Gallery + contribution docs\"]\n73\t    E002 --> E004\n74\t    E003 --> E004\n75\t```\n76\t\n77\tE002 is the root; all arrows point from dependency to dependent.\n78\t\n79\t## DAG Justification\n80\t\n81\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n82\t|------|------|-----------|\n83\t| E002 → E001 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The gallery code builds against the tutorial packaging format (its metadata schema) to list and launch tutorial packages. This is an API/contract-like artifact, not a configuration reference (image digests/URLs), so the consuming Implementation is serial after the format. |\n84\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The tutorials are packaged (metadata, pinned images) and tested (validation manifest) per the format; the content epic is a consumer of the format epic. |\n85\t| E001 ∥ E003 (no edge) | Rule 14 (different repos, no shared build artifact) | Gallery code and tutorial content live in different repos/components with no shared build artifact. The gallery is developed against the format (not against the specific tutorials); end-to-end launch of the curated set is an acceptance-criterion gate on both epics, not a DAG edge. |\n86\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes what was built; blocked by every Implementation epic. |\n87\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Contribution-process docs describe the packaging format and validation flow. |\n88\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Contribution-process docs describe tutorial authoring and testing. |\n89\t\n90\tCritical path: E002 → E001 → E004 (length 3).\n91\t\n92\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n93\t\n94\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement | Epic | Notes |\n95\t|-----|----------|-------------|------|-------|\n96\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Dashboard tutorial gallery from which a user can launch a tutorial into their project (workbench with notebook, or pipeline import) | RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Full coverage: gallery UI plus both launch flows. |\n97\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Six curated tutorials covering the core journeys, each tested against the current release | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Full coverage: all six journeys authored, packaged, and validated; workbench and pipeline-surface validation captured as ACs (passive components Notebooks and Data Science Pipelines). |\n98\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) so tutorials are versioned and testable independently of Dashboard releases | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Given its own epic — a standalone, separately schedulable deliverable (it does not share a UI or code surface with the P0 work; the gallery and tutorials are consumers of it). Epic priority promoted P1 → P0 by inheritance: it directly enables both P0 epics (see Health Warnings). |\n99\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers using the gallery and the contribution process | RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | `docs-authoring` epic; priority P1 derived from strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` per the docs-authoring priority exception. Contribution intake tooling is out of scope per the strategy; the process is documented only. |\n100\t\n101\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements; no HLR is co-located with\n102\ta higher-priority HLR in a single epic, so no priority-split bundling analysis\n103\tapplies.\n104\t\n105\t## Health Warnings\n106\t\n107\t- **Priority inversion (HLR-3 / E002)**: the strategy labels the tutorial\n108\t  packaging format P1, but both P0 HLRs build on it — the gallery code parses\n109\t  the format (Rule 13 edge) and the tutorials are packaged and validated per\n110\t  it (Rule 12 edge). By priority inheritance, E002 is promoted to P0 (an epic\n111\t  blocking all P0 work is implicitly P0). Flagged for human verification: if\n112\t  the product intent is that the gallery and tutorials can ship first against\n113\t  an interim ad-hoc packaging and the formal format lands later, decouple\n114\t  E002 from E001/E003 and restore its P1 priority; as written, the strategy's\n115\t  P0 \"tested against the current release\" requirement depends on the format's\n116\t  validation manifest, so the promotion is faithful to the stated scope.\n117\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n118\t  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria section, and no\n119\t  Non-Functional Requirements. Team assignments are inferred from\n120\t  `.context/architecture-context/` owning teams (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard,\n121\t  Notebooks → Workbenches); the documentation team is inferred as RHOAI\n122\t  Documentation. Epic acceptance criteria are derived from the HLRs. If the\n123\t  actual team model differs (e.g., the pipeline tutorial is owned/validated by\n124\t  RHOAI Pipelines rather than reviewed by them), reassign before scheduling.\n125\t- **Passive-component assumption**: Notebooks and Data Science Pipelines are\n126\t  classified passive — the strategy attributes all launch mechanics to the\n127\t  Dashboard, and `notebooks.md` confirms the Dashboard owns the spawn UI. If\n128\t  loading a notebook into a freshly spawned workbench turns out to require\n129\t  notebook-controller changes (rather than an image/startup mechanism the\n130\t  Dashboard drives), a notebook-controller epic would need to be added; the\n131\t  mechanism choice is an implementation detail for the Dashboard team, and the\n132\t  outcome is pinned by E001's acceptance criteria.\n133\t- **Planning note (epic size)**: the six curated tutorials epic (E003) is\n134\t  above the ~2-week guideline by scope arithmetic — six authored, packaged,\n135\t  and validated tutorials at roughly two to three days each. Kept as one\n136\t  logical change: the six form a single curated set with shared style,\n137\t  packaging setup, and one validation pass; a split would duplicate the\n138\t  packaging/validation setup and fragment curation consistency.\n139\t  **Re-split trigger**: re-split this epic if authoring exceeds the estimate —\n140\t  e.g., split the notebook tutorials from the pipeline tutorial, or deliver\n141\t  the set in two waves of three, once the first tutorials validate end to end.\n142\t\n143\t## Tiered Delivery\n144\t\n145\tNot applicable: the strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain\n146\ttiming; all work is in-platform.\n147\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-846866cdaf941267","agent_id":"a03c964834611fe0f","session_id":"d7ee07fb-436c-408b-a521-661a0ee22d32","uuid":"90065ece-a968-4abc-ba5b-0200cb38c229","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:39:55.887Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b67601ea04bcf91a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
